  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_019: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.639) has established that multiprofile + avgpool + weighted fusion is the strongest design so far. However, the RNA encoder has only been tested as pca_n2000 across all multimodal runs, leaving a critical design dimension unexplored. config_031 isolates the RNA encoder by swapping pca_n2000 for scvi_n200 while holding all other parameters at their best-known values (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted). This directly tests whether a learned latent RNA representation (scvi) can match or surpass a linear PCA projection in the multimodal setting. If scvi_n200 matches pca_n2000, the RNA encoder is not a bottleneck and we can focus on other dimensions; if it improves, we gain a new promising direction; if it degrades, we rule it out and can pivot to scgpt next. Under a limited budget, this single experiment reduces the most important remaining uncertainty (RNA encoder choice) within the already-validated high-performing region, making it the most information-dense next step."
}

